## 4. Expected, written down before the matrix is evaluated

  REAL column (the control): OLD sentence publishes, OLD gate true, NEW publishes — all three
  readings. If this column moves, the cure has become a blanket refusal and nothing below is
  a reading.

  KILL column, for each reading the kill hits:
    K1, K2, K3 — OLD sentence PUBLISHES while its OWN OLD GATE is FALSE (his finding), and the
                 NEW key is FALSE, so gate and sentence agree.
    K4         — OLD sentence publishes AND the OLD GATE passes too (it never carried D8), so
                 this row is strictly worse than the three he named, and the NEW key is FALSE.
  KILL column, for each reading the kill does NOT hit: nothing moves, in either spelling. That
  is what makes each kill specific to the conjunct it removes rather than a blanket crippling.

